{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessComplete","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessComplete","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessFinal","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdHrRatio"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessComplete.phiBProd_uniqueUpToScalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessComplete.phiBProd_uniqueUpToScalar","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdUniquenessComplete.lean#L30-L52","doc":"**`phiBProd` uniqueness up to scalar (substrate; `hr_ratio` + `hΦ₂_iso` discharged).**\nAny `FaddeevPhi` solution `Φ₁` at the substrate that is `FaddeevPhiStripGrowth` (comparable to\n`phiBProd`) and in meromorphic normal form, with the two dense periodicity loci, is proportional\nto `phiBProd`. The strip-growth `hbdd`, the zero-isolation, and the normal-form identity are all\ninternalized as theorems; only the loci-density hypotheses remain. ","signatureChunk":0}]}